sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    box rgb(239, 246, 255) PC1 ingestion and consumer
      participant SRC as live_replay_pc1<br/>managed_injector
      participant INGAPI as cms_ingestion_api<br/>private_boundary
      participant CONS as kafka_live_consumer_pc1
    end

    box rgb(236, 253, 245) PC1-PC3 Kafka cluster
      participant KRAW as measurement_live_v1<br/>3_partitions_RF3
      participant KCG as postgres_live_ingest_group<br/>lag_backlog
      participant KDLQ as measurement_dead_letter_v1
    end

    box rgb(238, 242, 255) AWS DB plane
      participant PG as cms_postgres
      participant LIVE as live_schema
      participant MART as mart_schema
      participant OPSQA as ops_qa_schema
      participant CAN as canonical_schema
    end

    box rgb(255, 247, 237) PC3 model serving
      participant FEAT as cms_anomaly_feature_worker
      participant MODEL as pmax_anomaly_scheduler
    end

    box rgb(245, 243, 255) PC1 promotion worker
      participant PROM as cms_canonical_promotion_worker
    end

    box rgb(245, 243, 255) Read surface
      participant API as cms_backend_api
    end

    SRC-->>INGAPI: next load resumes only through managed injector
    INGAPI->>KRAW: publish validated event envelope
    INGAPI-->>KDLQ: invalid payload is not written to PostgreSQL
    KRAW->>CONS: 3 partitions assigned to live consumer
    KCG->>CONS: track current offset, end offset, lag
    CONS->>PG: idempotent insert live.measurement_event
    PG->>LIVE: trigger policy / 1min / bucket queue
    LIVE->>MART: rollup and peak workers write features and model inputs
    LIVE->>FEAT: materialize 1h anomaly features
    MART->>MODEL: read mart.peak_feature_15min direct P-Max input
    MODEL->>MART: write pmax_forecast_15min and anomaly_warning_1h
    MODEL->>OPSQA: write inference logs and evidence packets
    LIVE->>PROM: eligible rows only after approval gate
    PROM->>CAN: controlled promotion to canonical tables
    LIVE-->>API: read-only live status and counts
    MART-->>API: read-only model-serving evidence
    OPSQA-->>API: read-only logs and QA packets

    Note over SRC,KCG: Kafka lag is backlog in offsets, not API latency. 2023 timestamps are intentional replay time.
    Note over MODEL,CAN: Direct P-Max input is mart.peak_feature_15min. Forecast and warning facts stay in mart, separate from canonical.
